{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/publications/political-party-spending-limits-independent-assessment-july-2026","content_id":"c7b38e12-82b9-4fa1-86e5-19b4c0156e96","description":"Correspondence between the Minister for Building Safety, Fire and Democracy and the Electoral Commission regarding an independent assessment of political party spending limits.","details":{"attachments":[{"accessible":false,"alternative_format_contact_email":"alternativeformats@communities.gov.uk","assets":[{"asset_manager_id":"6a5a2b7124d4d0ad06d946b7","filename":"Letter_to_Electoral_Commission_-_spending_limits_review_-_10_July_2026.pdf"}],"attachment_type":"file","command_paper_number":"","content_type":"application/pdf","file_size":645955,"filename":"Letter_to_Electoral_Commission_-_spending_limits_review_-_10_July_2026.pdf","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9479612","isbn":"","number_of_pages":2,"title":"Letter to the Electoral Commission: spending limits review (10 July 2026)","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a5a2b7124d4d0ad06d946b7/Letter_to_Electoral_Commission_-_spending_limits_review_-_10_July_2026.pdf"},{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9479613","isbn":"","title":"Letter to the Electoral Commission: spending limits review (10 July 2026)","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/political-party-spending-limits-independent-assessment-july-2026/letter-to-the-electoral-commission-spending-limits-review-10-july-2026-accessible-version"},{"accessible":false,"alternative_format_contact_email":"alternativeformats@communities.gov.uk","assets":[{"asset_manager_id":"6a5a260624d4d0ad06d946b1","filename":"Response_to_Minister_Dixon_regarding_spending_limit_review_-_13_Jul_2026.pdf"}],"attachment_type":"file","command_paper_number":"","content_type":"application/pdf","file_size":90425,"filename":"Response_to_Minister_Dixon_regarding_spending_limit_review_-_13_Jul_2026.pdf","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9479614","isbn":"","number_of_pages":1,"title":"Response to Minister Dixon: spending limit review (13 July 2026)","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a5a260624d4d0ad06d946b1/Response_to_Minister_Dixon_regarding_spending_limit_review_-_13_Jul_2026.pdf"},{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9479615","isbn":"","title":"Response to Minister Dixon: spending limit review (13 July 2026)","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/political-party-spending-limits-independent-assessment-july-2026/response-to-minister-dixon-spending-limit-review-13-july-2026-accessible-version"}],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>Under the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000, the government may amend spending limits through secondary legislation following recommendations from the Electoral Commission.</p>\n\n<p>To inform any future consideration of these limits, the government has asked the commission to review, by July 2027, the spending limits that apply to registered political parties and third-party campaigners at reserved elections, and to provide advice on whether they remain appropriate.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-17T14:00:00Z"}],"document_type_label":"Correspondence","emphasised_organisations":["1390d07f-12b3-4f55-9dd5-fec5fd9e3649"],"featured_attachments":["9479612","9479613","9479614","9479615"],"first_public_at":"2026-07-17T15:00:00.000+01:00","political":true,"tags":{"browse_pages":[]}},"document_type":"correspondence","first_published_at":"2026-07-17T15:00:00+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/publica